# Frontend git — human commits only

When working on ZeeFrame frontend roadmap phases (`frontend/docs/ROADMAP.md`):

1. **Never** run `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks in that message.
2. After **every** finished chunk (one checklist item or one agreed sub-step), end with a
   ready-to-paste Conventional Commit message, for example:

   ```text
   feat(web): add X-Request-ID to shared API client
   ```

3. Wait for the user to commit (or confirm continue) before starting the next chunk.
4. Prefer small, reviewable chunks — one concern per commit.
